> > But I don't see how there could be a balance issue with the branch
> > levels.  Without diving into the code, it doesn't seem like it would
> > be difficult to call up (for example) a mines branch bones when a
> > player gets to the appropriate level, and send each stair to a branch.
> 
> The only problem I can think of is that the branch may already exist,
> but it does seem easy enough to chcek for that and not use the bones
> level if so.

The levels on which branches are going to exist are predetermined at
game start, with the exception of the Ludios portal. So to implement
this, you'd want to give each branch level type its own boneid and
save it divorced from its depth, as special levels are.

The trouble with _that_ is that a branch can coincide with a special
level, and which gets preference? Duplication of special levels is a
Bad Idea, particularly in cases like Baalzebub's/Orcus' lair
containing Vlad's stairs. The only branch that's entirely clear of that
issue is the Mines stairs, and I can quite see why the DevTeam found
it easier just to say "no branching bones".

